    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mountunion/faculty/jobs/5465382/assistant-professor-biochemistry-chemistry": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Biochemistry & Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Biochemistry & Chemistry Location 1972 Clark Ave, Alliance, OH Job Type Faculty - Full Time Job Number 2025-00606 Department Academic Affairs Division Faculty Opening Date 08/28/2026 Description Benefits Description The department of Biochemistry, Chemistry, and Physics at the University of Mount Union, an ACS approved program, invites applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Biochemistry and Chemistry position to begin August 1, 2027. Our department of eleven faculty members strives for excellence in student learning through interactions in the classroom, working together in teaching labs, and undergraduate research experiences. We seek an educator-scholar who is passionate about teaching biochemistry and mentoring undergraduate students in a highly personalized learning environment. The successful candidate will join a collaborative department committed to excellence in teaching, undergraduate research, and student success. At Mount Union, faculty are valued not only for their disciplinary expertise but also for their ability to build meaningful relationships with students, foster intellectual curiosity, and create transformative educational experiences. This position offers the opportunity to directly influence the academic and professional development of undergraduate students pursuing careers in medicine, health sciences, industry, graduate study, and research. Responsibilities The primary teaching responsibility will be in biochemistry, including upper-level courses for biochemistry and chemistry. Depending on departmental needs and the successful candidate's expertise, additional teaching responsibilities may include general chemistry and/or organic chemistry. Candidates with expertise in polymer chemistry, materials chemistry, or related interdisciplinary applications of biochemistry are especially encouraged to apply. Research and Mentorship The successful candidate will develop and sustain an active research program that meaningfully engages undergraduate students. Mount Union values scholarship that prioritizes student development, providing opportunities for students to contribute to projects, present at professional conferences, co-author publications, and develop skills that prepare them for graduate study and professional careers. Applicants should describe how they would incorporate undergraduate researchers into their scholarly agenda and how their research interests could create opportunities for student learning and professional growth. Qualifications Ph.D. in Biochemistry, Chemistry, Polymer Chemistry, or a closely related field by the start date of employment. ABD will be considered. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. Strong potential to develop an active undergraduate research program. Ability to contribute to a collaborative and student-centered academic environment. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy and statement of research interests to www.mountunion.edu/employment . Three letters of recommendation will be requested of applicants after the initial review. Please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Scott Mason, masonss@mountunion.edu, with any questions. Review of applications will begin September 18, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Descriptive Information The University of Mount Union is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Mount Union prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, gender, gender identity or expression, sex, sexual orientation, religion, age, color, creed, national or ethnic origin, veteran status, marital or parental status, pregnancy, disability, or genetic information in student admissions, ?nancial aid, educational or athletic programs, or employment as now or may hereafter be required by University policy and federal or state law. The University of Mount Union, a private Midwestern institution founded in 1846, o?ers a rigorous and relevant academic program that is grounded in the liberal arts tradition. Mount Union’s more than 2,300 students can select from 56 broad-based and career speci?c undergraduate majors as well as master’s programs in physician assistant studies and education and a doctoral program in physical therapy. Known for its academic excellence and personal approach, the institution boasts a 13:1 student-faculty ratio and a curriculum delivered by dedicated faculty members, 87% of whom hold terminal degrees in their ?elds. Since 2005, nearly $110 million has been invested in the construction and renovation of modern facilities including a recreation center, apartment-style housing options, health, and medical sciences facility, and performing arts center. Primarily residential in nature, Mount Union’s picturesque 123-acre campus is located in Alliance, OH (Population23,000), within 80 miles of both Cleveland and Pittsburgh. The 162-acre Huston-Brumbaugh Nature Center is located six miles away. The University’s endowment is in excess of $141 million. The University strives to make its exceptional educational experience accessible to students of all ?nancial backgrounds. Its increasingly diverse campus community bene?ts from a student-centered approach and array of activities for cultural, civic, and social development. Students experience outstanding opportunities for success after graduation, both in the workforce and in graduate study. For more information, visit w ww.mountunion.edu For benefit eligible positions, the University of Mount Union provides a comprehensive benefits package including, but not limited to: free tuition, generous retirement contribution, medical/RX insurance through Aetna, dental and vision insurance, and group life and disability insurance. The University of Mount Union prides itself on its dedication to the health and well-being of its community and offers tobacco cessation resources, as all campus buildings and property are tobacco free. * Participation in most benefit programs is optional and participation is effective after the completion of the formal enrollment process and after the appropriate waiting periods. A detailed explanation of benefits offered for this position is provided by Human Resources during on-campus interviews. Employer University of Mount Union Address 1972 Clark Ave Alliance, Ohio, 44601 Phone (330) 829-6560 Website http://www.mountunion.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mountunion/faculty/jobs/5513110/visiting-assistant-professor-of-computer-science": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Computer Science Location 1972 Clark Ave, Alliance, OH Job Type Faculty - Full Time Job Number 2025-00620 Department Academic Affairs Division Faculty Opening Date 10/12/2026 Description Benefits Description The Department of Mathematics, Computer Science and Data Science at the University of Mount Union invites applications for a Visiting Assistant Professor of Computer Science position beginning January 1, 2027. This one-semester non-tenure appointment offers an exciting opportunity to join a growing and innovative computing program that includes majors in Computer Science, Multi-Platform Software Development, and Data Science & Analytics, as well as interdisciplinary offerings in Artificial Intelligence. We seek a dedicated educator with a passion for undergraduate teaching and student mentoring. The successful candidate will contribute to our mission of providing a personalized, hands-on educational experience that prepares students for careers in software development, artificial intelligence, data science, and related fields. Responsibilities The teaching assignment will be determined by departmental needs and the successful candidate's qualifications and may include courses such as: CSC 105 Introduction to Linux CSC 112 Introduction to Computer Science CSC 385 Using AI in Software Development CSC 482 Advanced Artificial Intelligence Systems DSC 230 Advanced Data Visualization DSC 360 Big Data Analytics The ideal candidate will demonstrate the ability to engage students through active learning, real-world applications, and emerging technologies while fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Excellence in teaching and enthusiasm for working closely with undergraduate students are essential. These courses are identified in the department's planned Spring 2027 teaching load. Qualifications Master's degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Information Technology, or a closely related field required. Ph.D. in Computer Science or a related discipline preferred. Professional experience in software development, data analytics, artificial intelligence, cloud computing, cybersecurity, or related fields is highly desirable. Demonstrated commitment to effective undergraduate teaching and student success. Descriptive Information The University of Mount Union is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Mount Union prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, gender, gender identity or expression, sex, sexual orientation, religion, age, color, creed, national or ethnic origin, veteran status, marital or parental status, pregnancy, disability, or genetic information in student admissions, financial aid, educational or athletic programs, or employment as now or may hereafter be required by university policy and federal or state laws. The University of Mount Union, a private Midwestern institution founded in 1846, offers a rigorous and relevant academic program that is grounded in the liberal arts. Mount Union's 2,300 students can select from 56 broad-based and career-specific undergraduate majors and three graduate programs. Known for its personal approach, the institution boasts a 13:1 student-faculty ratio. Mount Union's 123-acre campus, located in Alliance, Ohio, is primarily residential, and $110 million has been invested in its grounds and facilities since 2005. The University strives to make its education accessible to students of all financial backgrounds, and alumni experience outstanding opportunities for success. For more information, visit www.mountunion.edu Mount Union's Department of Mathematics and Computer Science offers majors in Computer Science and Multi-Platform Software Development, with approximately 45 students in these majors last year. The Department also offers minors in Computer Science, Database Management, Computer and Network Security, and Web Design, and contributes to the University's major and minor in Data Science and Analytics. Most courses in the Computer Science program meet in a computer teaching lab reserved for the program's exclusive use, providing effective support for a hands-on instructional approach. Candidates should provide a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy and contact information for three professional references to the Computer Science Search Committee. Electronic applications are required and can be submitted online at www.mountunion.edu/employment. Please direct any questions to the search committee chair, Professor Blase Cindric, at cindricbb@mountunion.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately, and will continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. For benefit eligible positions, the University of Mount Union provides a comprehensive benefits package including, but not limited to: free tuition, generous retirement contribution, medical/RX insurance through Aetna, dental and vision insurance, and group life and disability insurance. The University of Mount Union prides itself on its dedication to the health and well-being of its community and offers tobacco cessation resources, as all campus buildings and property are tobacco free. * Participation in most benefit programs is optional and participation is effective after the completion of the formal enrollment process and after the appropriate waiting periods. A detailed explanation of benefits offered for this position is provided by Human Resources during on-campus interviews. Employer University of Mount Union Address 1972 Clark Ave Alliance, Ohio, 44601 Phone (330) 829-6560 Website http://www.mountunion.edu/ Apply"
    },
