      "description": "Assistant Professor, Business Management, NTT Location 1972 Clark Ave, Alliance, OH Job Type Faculty - Full Time Job Number 2025-00622 Department Academic Affairs Division Faculty Opening Date 10/28/2026 Description Benefits Description The school of Business at the University of Mount Union invites applications for a Non-Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Business Management. The School of Business at the University of Mount Union is comprised of undergraduate majors in accounting, finance, management, marketing, and sport business. Additionally, it offers minors in accounting, business administration, economics, entrepreneurship, leadership studies, marketing, and sport business. The School of Business offers a breadth of knowledge and career specific study through a robust curriculum and experiential learning opportunities. Undergraduate programs currently offered in the School of business are accredited through the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP) Baccalaureate/Graduate Degree Board of Commissioners and the Commission on Sport Management Accreditation (COSMA). Responsibilities Responsibilities will include teaching a variety of undergraduate business courses including introduction to Business, Business Communication, and management related courses such as Management Principles, Operations Management, Project Management, or Human Resources Management. Additionally, the candidate will be expected to serve as an advisor and mentor for undergraduate majors, support students in research, and participate in research and service activities. Qualifications Qualifications include an earned doctorate in business, or closely related discipline. ABD may be considered. We seek candidates with demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and belonging. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and teaching philosophy to www.mountunion.edu/employment . Three letters of recommendation will 